# Switching the Split Inbox's sides at 100,000 messages (the fork's phase C,
# docs/superhuman/split.md "UI"): Tab and Shift+Tab, from the key press to the first frame
# painted with the other side's rows, with conversation rows in Focused, with message rows,
# and in Split. Each switch must adopt the other side's view, opened ahead; what is left is
# GTK's reset of a long list and the frame's paint. It prints the numbers, as perf-list does:
# the bar (50 ms) is read from them on a quiet machine (split.md "Measured"), so the medians
# are held only to 1 s here, which a switch gone badly wrong passes.
#
# Not part of tools/ci.sh (perf-*): it needs a release build and the perf-list fixture store:
#   cargo build --release -p pronto -p sealwax-fixtures
#   tools/headless.sh 36 target/release/pronto --self-test tests/selftest/perf-split.sealwax-test
# The store is imported once into target/perf-list/data (about 40 s, 1.1 GB), as perf-list does,
# and reused while it is there.

desktop tiling
layout-defaults app
store-dir $DIR/../../target/perf-list/data
fixtures --count 100000 --seed 1
resize 1440 900
list-wait
split-inbox on
list-wait
assert-split-side important
focus list
sleep 1500
measure-split Tab 20 1000
measure-split <Shift>Tab 10 1000
grouping messages
list-wait
sleep 800
measure-split Tab 10 1000
grouping conversations
list-wait
view-mode split
sleep 800
measure-split Tab 10 1000
